# Q1: How would a human perform this motion? (One sentence)
A human brings their palms together in front of their chest, fingers pointing up, and then performs a slight bow of the head and upper body.
# Q2: Pose Candidates Comparison. Rank at least 2 pose configurations (torso_height, arm_position, gripper_orientation, head, left_arm, x/y/z) and state the winner and why—do NOT pick presets from gesture names alone.
Pose A: `arm_position: "in"`, `left_arm: "mirror"`, `gripper_orientation: "vertical"`. This brings both arms inward across the chest to meet at the centerline, correctly forming the "palms together" shape. Pose B: `arm_position: "front"`, `left_arm: "mirror"`. This extends both arms forward, resulting in a wide-apart gesture unsuitable for this cue. Winner is Pose A because it correctly and efficiently creates the central hands-together posture.
# Q3: Structure Comparison. Compare 2+ full primitive sequences (e.g., M1: pose > movement > pose vs M2: pose > path > path). State the winner and why—**prioritize movement/path beats that express the cue**, not pose-only tweaks.
M1: `pose` (hands together) -> `movement` (bow with torso+head) -> `pose` (hold bow). M2: `pose` (arms open) -> `path` (bring hands together) -> `movement` (bow). Winner is M1 because it establishes the iconic hand posture immediately and focuses the main action on the respectful bow, making the gesture clear and concise.
# Q4: Context Reinforcement. Compare 2+ micro-timing choices (speed, repetition, hold_time, torso/head expression) that make the gesture read stronger and pick the best one.
Timing A: Fast bow (speed > 2.0) with no hold. This would feel rushed and insincere. Timing B: Slow bow (speed ~0.8) with a distinct hold (~1.5s) at the end. This conveys respect, deliberation, and gratitude. Winner is Timing B, as the slower tempo and hold are critical for the emotional expression of thankfulness.
